W: 1 O Splendor of God&apos;s glory bright,
W: O Thou that bringest light from light,
W: O Light of Light, light&apos;s living spring,
W: O Day, all days illumining:
W:
W: 2 Come, very Sun of truth and love;
W: Pour down Thy radiance from above
W: And shed the Holy Spirit&apos;s ray
W: On all we think or do or say.
W:
W: 3 With prayer the Father we implore:
W: O Father, glorious evermore,
W: We plead with Thee for grace and pow&apos;r
W: To conquer in temptation&apos;s hour,
W:
W: 4 To guide whate&apos;er we nobly do,
W: With love all envy to subdue,
W: To give us grace our wrongs to bear,
W: To make ill fortune turn to fair.
W:
W: 5 On Christ, the true bread, let us feed;
W: Let Him to us be drink indeed;
W: And let us taste with joyfulness
W: The Holy Spirit&apos;s plenteousness.
W:
W: 6 All laud to God the Father be;
W: All praise, eternal Son, to Thee;
W: All glory to the Spirit raise
W: In equal and unending praise.
W: Alleluia!</miscellaneous-field>
